          run: "echo \"CARGO_HOME=$RUNNER_TEMP/cargo\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\necho \"RUSTUP_HOME=$RUNNER_TEMP/rustup\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n# INTERIM sccache transport (operator 2026-06-01 override; \"disregard the memo for now\").\n# Right-way fix is the modeled cache_interface projection consumer (dsl/std/cache_interface.dag\n# sccache_local_facts; src/v4/workflow/ci.dag cache-projection note) -- NOT this hand-wire.\n# The runner provides an ISOLATED, ghrunner-owned sccache via systemd env (SCCACHE_DIR +\n# SCCACHE_SERVER_UDS, ctrl#1419). Do NOT hardcode SCCACHE_SERVER_UDS here: a job/step-level\n# env beats the runner default, so pinning the old shared socket forces EACCES and keeps\n# sccache inert. Inherit the runner's socket; only flip RUSTC_WRAPPER on. The server starts\n# LAZILY (sccache creates the socket on the first rustc call), so the socket does NOT exist yet\n# at this pre-cargo step -- so we gate in two stages. (1) the socket's\n# PARENT DIR must be writable (runner provisions it ghrunner:ghrunner 0755,\n# ctrl#1419); a missing/unwritable dir -> cold build. (2) actively\n# health-probe the server: `--start-server` is idempotent (no-op if up,\n# else starts + WARMS it) and `--show-stats` forces the SAME client->server\n# round-trip the compile will use. Why (2): the dir test only proves sccache\n# COULD start, not that the server is reachable -- a lazily-started server\n# from a prior job can be mid-idle-shutdown exactly as this job's first\n# `rustc -vV` connects, failing the build HARD with \"failed to read response\n# header\" (observed 2026-06-04, run 26985377093). Probing here catches a\n# sick/unreachable server and degrades to a cold build (::warning) instead\n# of a hard mid-build failure. The `&&` chain runs in an `if` condition, so\n# a probe failure under `set -e` selects the cold branch, never aborts.\n# Fails SAFE at every stage; dissolve-on-arrival (real fix: ci.dag cache projection).\nif [ -n \"$SCCACHE_SERVER_UDS\" ] && [ -w \"$(dirname \"$SCCACHE_SERVER_UDS\")\" ] \\\n     && sccache --start-server >/dev/null 2>&1 \\\n     && sccache --show-stats >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n  echo \"CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\nelse\n  echo \"::warning::sccache server (SCCACHE_SERVER_UDS=${SCCACHE_SERVER_UDS:-unset}) absent, unwritable, or unreachable; building cold\"\nfi\n",
